MidnightBSD reports itself as "midnightbsd" to the JVM, which rules_go
turns into a GOOS of the same name; there is no such GOOS.  Go itself has
no MidnightBSD port: mports ships the FreeBSD build, and the kernel runs
FreeBSD binaries, so the freebsd SDK is the one to use.  CI only.

--- a/go/private/sdk.bzl
+++ b/go/private/sdk.bzl
@@ -467,6 +467,8 @@ def detect_host_platform(ctx):
         goos = "darwin"
     elif goos.startswith("windows"):
         goos = "windows"
+    elif goos == "midnightbsd":
+        goos = "freebsd"
 
     goarch = ctx.os.arch
     if goarch == "aarch64":
